    "criticality": "high",
    "description": "Bad twin of glassbox-ot-agent: the demo configuration as first built, with its shortcuts and the gaps a first version typically has. The agent's MCP server got an execute_command tool that calls the command broker directly; Jetson B writes its PLC straight from cloud-to-device messages without validating them, and Jetson A also bridges line B setpoints; alarm text reaches the model unscreened; approvals are signed under a shared service identity; one SQL database serves both lines without row-level security, and neither the custom agent nor the configured database has a supplier or development assessment on file. The model is called without the AI gateway over a public endpoint, SQL is public with platform keys, personas sign in without MFA and without a WAF, the Jetsons have no secure boot, traces are kept 90 days, drafted reports are not marked as AI-generated and no incident reporting path is defined.",
